          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "Perth has a strong ecosystem of Microsoft Solutions Partners and boutique AI consultancies, driven largely by local demand across mining, engineering, professional services, and logistics. \n\nSeveral consultancies in Perth specialize in **Microsoft Copilot Studio**, **autonomous/agentic AI**, and **practical workflow automation** for mid-market businesses:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Dedicated Mid-Market & Power Platform Specialists\n\n* **Opticloud Solutions** *(Perth CBD - St Georges Terrace)*\n  * **Focus:** A dedicated Perth-based consultancy specifically focused on Microsoft 365, Power Platform, and AI agents.\n  * **Best For:** Mid-market businesses looking for practical, high-ROI workflow automations. They build custom low-code agents via Copilot Studio, tie them into Power Automate/Power Apps, and integrate them with SharePoint, Dataverse, or ERPs.\n* **Novata Solutions** *(Perth)*\n  * **Focus:** Long-standing Perth Microsoft specialist focusing on business applications, workflow modernisation, and AI integration.\n  * **Best For:** Organizations transitioning from traditional forms/SharePoint workflows into agentic processes. They specialize in deploying Copilot Studio agents grounded in internal documentation, automating standard operating procedures, and managing back-office approvals.\n* **BIZ-LYNX Technology** *(Perth)*\n  * **Focus:** Practical AI adoption, Copilot readiness, and business process automation.\n  * **Best For:** Mid-sized operations that need to cut through AI hype. They assess Microsoft 365/Dynamics licensing, prepare security boundaries, and build grounded Copilot Studio bots to handle internal ticketing, HR onboarding, and CRM updates.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Boutique AI-Native Automation Consultancies\n\n* **Delivr** *(Perth)*\n  * **Focus:** An AI-native consultancy built around rapid mid-market delivery (delivering working systems in weeks rather than months).\n  * **Best For:** Companies needing hybrid architecture (e.g., orchestrating Microsoft Power Platform alongside Python/Azure AI agents or external APIs). They frequently work in industrial and operational mid-market contexts.\n* **Austin Technology** *(Subiaco)*\n  * **Focus:** Mid-market IT managed services and automation consultancy.\n  * **Best For:** Practical, day-to-day workflow workflows. They implement Copilot Studio agents grounded in organizational handbooks and policies, configure system connectors, and implement the necessary AI governance policies to prevent internal data leakage.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Tier-1 & Established Microsoft Solutions Partners (Perth Hubs)\n\nIf your mid-market business has complex compliance needs, ERP ties (Business Central/F&O), or anticipates scaling to enterprise:\n\n* **Arinco** *(Perth Office)*\n  * **Focus:** One of Australia’s premier Microsoft cloud/AI consultancies with deep capability in Azure AI Foundry, Power Platform, and Copilot Studio.\n  * **Best For:** Multi-agent architectures, security boundaries, and advanced custom extensions where standard out-of-the-box templates fall short.\n* **SOCO** *(Perth Hub)*\n  * **Focus:** ASX-listed Microsoft Solutions Partner with a strong presence across WA government, resources, and corporate mid-market.\n  * **Best For:** End-to-end Copilot readiness, secure data foundation (SharePoint/Purview), and scaling agentic workflows directly inside Dynamics 365 and Microsoft 365.\n* **Velrada** *(Perth HQ - St Georges Terrace)*\n  * **Focus:** Historically Perth’s premier Business Applications powerhouse (now part of NRI).\n  * **Best For:** Complex field operations, scheduling, and multi-departmental Copilot Studio orchestration.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look For When Engaging a Consultant\n\nWhen vetting a partner for **Copilot Studio and mid-market AI automation**, ensure they address:\n1. **Security & Information Architecture:** Copilot Studio relies on your tenant’s data. If your SharePoint or Dataverse permissions are not strictly scoped, agents will surface confidential documents to unauthorised staff. A reliable consultant must always offer a **security/readiness audit** first.\n2. **Beyond Low-Code:** Verify if they understand **Power Automate Desktop (RPA)** and custom REST connectors. The most practical mid-market agents require triggering actions in non-Microsoft tools (e.g., MYOB, Xero, Jobpac, or Jira).\n3. **Change Management:** Look for consultants who conduct team enablement so your staff actually adopt the agents instead of bypassing them.",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
          ],
